WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.600
Viagra was discovered by accident,

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:04.600
but its impact has been huge.

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:09.200
The search for something
to help men get it up

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:10.960
is as old as history itself.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.360
From eating roasted wolf penis,

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:14.960
to electric shocks,

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.720
to silicone implants
inserted into the shaft.

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:19.680
You name it, it's been tried.

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:23.480
But the story of how Viagra
was discovered was quite unexpected.

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:25.360
It's the early 1990s.

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:27.680
A number of men
in a trial for sildenafil -

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:29.360
a drug to treat angina -

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:31.720
report unanticipated side effects.

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:35.360
Erections. Lots of them.

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:36.920
The urban myth -
which happens to be true -

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:38.280
is that the men who had it

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:40.480
refused to return
their unused tablets,

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:42.880
because their sex lives
improved so much.

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:45.320
The first clinical trials
for it as an erection drug

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:47.600
are held in Swansea in 1994.

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:50.880
And it was clear then,
after the first patient,

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:52.600
that we had something special then.

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:55.240
So we had these ordinary,
middle-aged, Swansea men

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:57.720
able to have sex
for the first time in years,

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:00.080
after just taking a tablet.

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:03.080
And four years later,
Viagra - as it's now known -

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:04.480
comes to market.

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:07.360
Before the '90s,
the condition Viagra can treat

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.400
was known as "impotence".

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:12.840
Which is not a great word if
you're trying to sell a drug to men,

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:15.760
as it literally means
"lacking in power".

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:18.680
So the marketing team
hones in on a new term,

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:20.760
"erectile dysfunction",

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:25.400
and enlists key figures - including
Brazilian superstar footballer Pele,

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:28.160
and US presidential candidate
Bob Dole -

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:31.040
to open up and normalise
erection difficulties,

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:33.200
particularly for older men.

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:34.880
Viagra, the little blue diamond,

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:38.400
becomes one of
the fastest-selling drugs ever.

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:40.600
Men who'd struggled for years
with their erections,

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:42.680
but had been too afraid
to talk about it,

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:44.800
finally had something
that could help.

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:46.040
Just like erections,

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:49.280
studies into erection difficulties
can vary widely,

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:51.240
and are often unreliable.

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:54.920
One UK study found that
around 8% of men under 44

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:58.040
had had trouble
getting, or keeping, an erection.

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:00.440
Older men are far more likely
to be affected -

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:04.680
the figure rises to 30%
for men aged 65-74.

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:06.960
It's strongly associated
with health conditions,

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:09.440
like cardiovascular disease
and diabetes,

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:12.320
and also depression and life events
such as unemployment

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:14.440
and relationship difficulties.

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:16.480
Some argue Viagra
was as revolutionary

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:18.720
as the introduction
of the contraceptive pill.

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:20.480
But others disagree.

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:22.960
Instead of opening up
discussions around sex,

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:25.080
critics say Viagra has doubled down

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:27.640
on a really narrow idea
of what sex is.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:30.960
And reinforced
stereotypes about masculinity.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:32.440
Take the porn industry.

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:35.560
Before Viagra, male actors
would be chosen for their ability

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:37.720
to get hard and stay hard.

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:39.800
They were known as "woodsmen"!

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:42.200
But porn films were more realistic,

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:46.480
and often featured flaccid penises,
too. Because that's the reality.

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:48.560
Viagra turbo-charged all that.

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:53.760
Now it's younger, harder,
more athletic men.

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:57.040
Sex scenes are longer, rougher,
and involve more penetration.

00:02:57.080 --> 00:03:00.120
This adds to the expectation
that men's role in sex

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:02.720
is to get hard and perform.

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:06.160
So, many younger men
have performance anxiety.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:09.200
Stress plays a huge role
in inhibiting erections

00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:12.160
so, ironically,
stressing about erections

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:14.080
can make it harder to get hard.

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:16.680
It's actually normal
not to be hard all the time.

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:18.520
And when we talk about hard,

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:20.120
how hard do we mean?

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:23.520
Not all sexual activities
require a rock-hard penis.

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:26.080
And if we really want a hard penis
all the time,

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:28.600
we can buy one
and keep it in a drawer.

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:31.640
If you want to have
a good sex life,

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:33.880
then talking about sex
with your partner,

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:36.360
trying new things
and being comfortable

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:41.040
about what your body can and can't
do, is the best way to get there.

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:43.520
So did Viagra change the world?

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:46.200
Or just double down on how it was?

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:49.320
And just as sildenafil -
to use its clinical name again -

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:53.000
was never originally intended
as a drug to help with hard-ons,

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:55.680
it could have some
other potential uses too.

00:03:55.720 --> 00:03:57.720
One small study
found promising evidence

00:03:57.760 --> 00:03:59.760
to suggest it could help
with period pain.

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:03.000
But efforts to explore this further
have never been funded.

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:06.680
And early studies suggest
it could potentially be useful

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:08.360
in treating Alzheimer's.

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:12.000
So could Viagra change the world
in a totally different way?

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:13.600
Watch this space.

